-- Q3829: IT General Controls [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Program change management and version control","System capacity and performance management","Batch job scheduling and automation controls","Logical access controls and data protection"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Per NIST SP 800-53 Rev. 5, control families AC (Access Control) and SC (System and Communications Protection), DLP controls address logical access and data protection by monitoring data in motion, at rest, and in use to prevent unauthorized transmission of sensitive information.
Wrong (A): Program change management governs software modifications and version control, not data movement restrictions.
Wrong (B): System capacity management addresses resource availability and performance thresholds, not sensitive data transfers.
Wrong (C): Batch job scheduling automates routine processing tasks and has no role in monitoring or restricting data transfers.$EXPL$
