-- Q3831: IT General Controls [hard/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Automated processes will stop functioning due to expired service account passwords","Service accounts will automatically lock after the defined inactivity period","The organization will face immediate regulatory fines for password non-compliance","Stale credentials increase compromise risk, especially if exposed in a prior breach"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Per NIST SP 800-63B and AICPA TSC CC6.1, service accounts with static, unchanging passwords create an indefinite exposure window if credentials are compromised. An attacker retains access until the password is rotated, and organizations should use automated rotation or managed identities.
Wrong (A): Service account passwords typically do not expire like user passwords; automated processes would not stop functioning on their own.
Wrong (B): Service accounts are generally exempt from automatic lockout policies designed for interactive user accounts.
Wrong (C): Regulatory fines are not an immediate or automatic consequence of stale passwords; the primary risk is unauthorized access.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3831;

