-- Q3841: IT Audit Frameworks [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Risk avoidance, because the insurance eliminates the ransomware threat entirely","Risk mitigation, because the insurance reduces the likelihood of future ransomware attacks","Risk transfer, because financial impact shifts to the insurer while residual risks remain","Risk acceptance, because purchasing insurance means tolerating the risk without controls"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under COBIT 2019 EDM03 (Ensured Risk Optimization), purchasing cyber insurance is classified as risk transfer because it shifts the financial impact to a third-party insurer. Residual risks such as the deductible, operational disruption, and reputational damage remain with the organization.
Wrong (A): Risk avoidance eliminates the risk-creating activity entirely; insurance does not eliminate the ransomware threat.
Wrong (B): Insurance does not reduce the likelihood of an attack occurring; it only addresses financial consequences after an event.
Wrong (D): Risk acceptance means deliberately tolerating a risk without additional controls; purchasing insurance is an active risk response, not passive acceptance.$EXPL$
