-- Q3845: IT Audit Frameworks [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The objective is fully met because the preventive control alone satisfies the access restriction requirement","The auditor cannot evaluate until the organization completes the missing access reviews retroactively","The objective is partially met; the missing detective control leaves potential unauthorized changes undetected","The gap has no impact because detective controls are optional and do not affect objective achievement"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Per AT-C Section 205.35, control objectives require both suitable design and operating effectiveness. While RBAC limits initial access, the missing quarterly access review means unauthorized access changes during two quarters may have gone undetected, weakening the overall control environment.
Wrong (A): A single preventive control rarely satisfies an objective alone; detective controls provide essential compensating assurance against configuration drift.
Wrong (B): The auditor evaluates based on evidence available during the examination period and does not wait for retroactive remediation.
Wrong (D): Detective controls are integral to control environments; their absence directly affects the auditor''s assessment of objective achievement.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3845;

