-- Q3853: IT Audit Frameworks [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["All IT areas receive equal audit attention regardless of their assessed risk level","The scope is determined randomly to ensure complete auditor independence","Only areas that failed the previous audit cycle are included in scope","Higher-risk areas receive more audit attention while lower-risk areas receive less"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Per COBIT 2019 MEA03 and ISACA ITAF Standard 1202, a risk-based audit approach allocates resources based on assessed risk levels. Areas with higher inherent risk, greater control risk, or significant prior findings receive more intensive procedures, ensuring effort focuses where it provides the most value.
Wrong (A): Equal attention regardless of risk ignores the fundamental principle of risk-based auditing and wastes resources on low-risk areas.
Wrong (B): Random scope determination does not address risk and could miss critical high-risk areas requiring audit coverage.
Wrong (C): Limiting scope to prior failures ignores newly emerging risks and areas that have not been previously tested.$EXPL$
